Remote File Command Server in C.


* ** the client can create/ read / write / append / delete a file to the server. he can only work in a spasific folder in the file system, every atteamp to get out of this folder will be blocked.

* ** the allowed command is action filename text(only for write action)

* ** inside the permited folder there will be 6 sub folders that the client can work on, therefore the client need to enter the next path: userX_Folder/file_name


* ** Multi threaded Archutecture (Thread Pool). managing new clients that by adding them to the circular queue

* ** Writer control. a file can have multiple readrs, it can have a reader and a writer. but it cant have a writer and a writer. every time there is a new writer he will be added to a dynamic array that contains all the active writers in the system. every file can have only till one writer

binary application protocol. every packet that go will have a header the header will conatin a magic num is the client/server will know the recieved from legit source. every packet to translate from host to network and network to host

* ** clean socket life style. wrapper functions writeAll and readAll will transmit all the bytes in the buffer until there is not more.

to run the program you need to run the two next compile commands


gcc -Wall -Wextra -pthread     -I Server/include     -I Shared_modules/include     Server/src/*.c     Shared_modules/src/net_utilities.c     Shared_modules/src/protocol.c     -o bin/server


gcc -Wall -Wextra     -I Client/include     -I Shared_modules/include     Client/src/cli.c     Client/src/command_parsing.c     Shared_modules/src/net_utilities.c     Shared_modules/src/protocol.c     -o bin/client




and the run the two commands
./bin/server
./bin/client
